cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "FuzzyDiary: An open-source framework for morphology-aware and traceable linguistic summarization of clinical time series"
abstract: >-
  FuzzyDiary is an open-source Python framework for protoform-based,
  morphology-aware linguistic summarization of univariate time series. It
  couples Ramer-Douglas-Peucker simplification with a configurable catalogue of
  morphological events and fuzzy protoform evaluation, driven by a single YAML
  configuration, and produces a self-contained interactive HTML report in which
  every generated statement is linked to the segment of the signal that
  supports it.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ASIATIC257UJA/fuzzydiary"
keywords:
  - linguistic summarization
  - fuzzy protoforms
  - time series
  - explainability
  - clinical monitoring
  - continuous glucose monitoring
